      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30 – 90 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-regime status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N4</span>
          <span class="fc-category">regime</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Mojtaba Khamenei make a confirmed, independently verified public in-person appearance before EOD 2026-10-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">33%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 33% (2026-08-27)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">No material movement. Pakistan Army Chief General Asim Munir visited Tehran Aug 24-25, meeting with President Pezeshkian, parliament, the Supreme National Security Council, and foreign and interior ministries (Haaretz, Al Jazeera). Haaretz reported Munir expected to meet "people close to Khamenei" — a confirmed direct encounter with Mojtaba Khamenei was not documented in TIER1 or OSINT sources as of Aug 28. Iranian state media released undated photographs and image promises ~Aug 10, which do not satisfy N4's resolution criteria (two TIER1 international outlets with video, or a foreign government delegation confirming in-person contact). President Pezeshkian's reported 7-hour meeting uses an Iranian government source, explicitly excluded by the resolution criteria.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>Video confirmed by two+ TIER1 international outlets (non-Iranian state media) showing Mojtaba Khamenei conducting official duties in person; OR official foreign government diplomatic delegation publicly confirming an in-person meeting with Khamenei in an attributed statement accepted by at least one TIER1 outlet.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 outlets outside Iranian state media, or one TIER1 outlet plus an attributed foreign government official statement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Written statements, audio recordings, or still photographs without corroborating video or foreign diplomatic attestation do not qualify. Iranian state media alone does not satisfy "independently verified." Event attended exclusively by IRGC or Iranian officials does not qualify without credible non-Iranian third-party witness.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Assembly of Experts formal plenary in Tehran requiring Khamenei address</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Oman or Qatar FM confirmed travel to Tehran for meeting with named leadership</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Foreign government official public statement confirming in-person contact with Mojtaba Khamenei</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N5</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Israel's October 27, 2026 general election be officially postponed to a date beyond November 10, 2026?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">7%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 7% (2026-08-27)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-28</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">No material movement. The Israeli Central Elections Commission has confirmed October 27, 2026 as the election date. No Attorney General postponement opinion, Security Cabinet extraordinary conditions declaration, or Knesset Speaker request to the CEC has been documented. Opposition leader Bennett publicly stated "nobody will be allowed to postpone" the election. The supermajority threshold (80 MKs) required for formal postponement is not achievable given the current 48-49 seat caretaker bloc (Haaretz, Aug 26).</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>Official announcement by Israeli CEC or Knesset standing committee order establishing a new election date later than November 10, 2026, published in the Official Gazette (Reshumot) or reported by two TIER1 outlets with direct CEC citation.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reshumot official publication or two TIER1 outlets citing official CEC announcement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Cabinet deliberations or petitions without formal date change do not qualify. Postponement to any date on or before November 10 does not qualify. Postponement later reversed to October 27 resolves AMBIGUOUS.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Attorney General extraordinary legal opinion on postponement permissibility</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Security Cabinet formal declaration of extraordinary security conditions</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Knesset Speaker written request to CEC for postponement review</span>
        </div>
