        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N6</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the IAEA formally report completion of Iran's down-blending of all ≥60%-enriched uranium stocks to ≤5% enrichment before EOD 2027-03-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">10%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −6pp from 16% (2026-08-27)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2027-03-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">IAEA verification and monitoring activities in Iran have been suspended since February 28, 2026 (GOV/2026/8). Resolution requires three sequential prerequisites: (1) restoration of IAEA continuous monitoring access, (2) confirmed active downblending under IAEA supervision, (3) IAEA Director General formal completion report — all three remain absent. Iran's 60%-enriched uranium stock was approximately 440.9 kg per the last known IAEA estimate. No downblending under IAEA supervision has been confirmed. The June MOU expired August 17 without a successor framework; no evidence of IAEA access restoration appeared in the Aug 26-28 search window. p revised 0.16 → 0.10.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>IAEA DG report, Board of Governors formal document, or IAEA Secretariat statement explicitly confirming FULL completion — not partial progress — of Iran's downblending of all ≥60% LEU stocks to ≤5% under IAEA continuous monitoring, before EOD 2027-03-01.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IAEA.org official publication; TIER1 wire with direct attribution to IAEA DG statement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Progress reports, partial-completion milestones, or IAEA access restoration without confirmed full completion do not qualify. A stockpile reduction without completion to ≤5% does not qualify. If nuclear stocks are physically destroyed and IAEA cannot verify compliance, resolve AMBIGUOUS pending IAEA Board assessment.</dd>
        </dl>
