  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>Oman Foreign Minister Badr al-Busaidi arrived in Tehran on August 25 for consultations with Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi. The two ministers jointly published a communiqué — simultaneously posted on Oman's Ministry of Foreign Affairs official website (fm.gov.om/en/53722/) and Iranian state channels — establishing a "joint temporary navigational corridor through the Strait of Hormuz" and a "joint project to clear the Strait of mines." A joint working group was designated to continue technical negotiations toward a permanent corridor arrangement. Bloomberg (TIER1, Aug 25) and Al Jazeera (TIER1, Aug 26) independently confirmed the bilateral framework announcement from both foreign ministries. → moved <span class="cite">N2</span>, <span class="cite">N7</span></p>

      <p>The United States completed a 28th consecutive night without conducting airstrikes on internationally recognized Iranian land territory, per the Day 181-182 OPREP compiled by GlobalSecurity.org (Aug 26-27). Secretary of State Rubio communicated to allied foreign ministries on August 25 that "no new American strikes on Iran are expected for the time being," according to Reuters. No CENTCOM press releases documenting new Iran land strikes appeared in the August 26-28 search window. The pause began during the Islamabad MOU process and continued through and beyond its August 17 expiry without an announced termination. → supports <span class="cite">N1</span> without move</p>

      <p>Pakistan Army Chief General Asim Munir returned to Tehran on August 24-25, conducting bilateral meetings with President Pezeshkian, members of parliament, the Supreme National Security Council, and the foreign and interior ministries (Haaretz, Aug 24; Al Jazeera, Aug 25). Pakistani officials described "significant progress" in Iran-US dialogue to Al Jazeera on August 25. Haaretz reported that Munir expected to meet "people close to Khamenei" during the visit; a confirmed direct encounter with Mojtaba Khamenei was not documented in available TIER1 or OSINT sources as of August 28. → supports <span class="cite">N4</span> without move</p>

      <p>ICE Brent crude front-month settled at approximately $88.22 per barrel on August 28 (TradingEconomics), remaining $51.78 below the N3 threshold of $140.00/bbl. Straits.live recorded 3 commercial vessel transits through the Strait of Hormuz on August 23 — approximately 3.5% of the pre-war baseline of 85 transits per day. The Baltic Dirty Tanker Index recorded no week-on-week increase exceeding 15% in the Aug 21-28 period. Saudi Arabia has not announced emergency production capacity deployment above 11.5 million barrels per day. → supports <span class="cite">N3</span> without move, supports <span class="cite">N7</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 4. SCENARIO MAP ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Scenario Map
      <span class="meta">Computed from Forecast Board · 1 sentence per scenario</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="scenario-map">
      <div class="prob-bar-container">
        <div class="prob-bar prob-escalation" style="width:12%;">Esc 12%</div>
        <div class="prob-bar prob-status" style="width:53%;">Protracted 53%</div>
        <div class="prob-bar prob-deescalation" style="width:35%;">De-esc 35%</div>
      </div>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (12%):</strong> Driven by residual N1 probability (8%) and a catastrophic oil-price shock scenario (N3 at 7%); requires a US decision to resume strikes while the Oman corridor framework collapses and IRGC enforcement resumes tanker seizures.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (53%):</strong> The dominant scenario: the Iran-Oman corridor framework (N2 YES) exists on paper but Hormuz remains near-shutdown at 3 transits/day, IAEA monitoring is suspended (N6 at 10%), and the 28-night strike pause holds without a formal successor to the expired MOU — a frozen diplomatic stalemate with sporadic tactical moves on both sides.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (35%):</strong> Anchored by N2 (resolved YES), N7 (30% probability of Hormuz transit recovery by Sep 21), and the active Pakistan backchannel; the Oman corridor agreement provides the operational mechanism for a broader de-escalation if shipping industry, IAEA, and US-Iran diplomatic tracks advance in September.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iranian state broadcaster IRIB and Tasnim News framed the Iran-Oman communiqué (Aug 25-26) as a confirmation of Iran's "principled stance" on Hormuz sovereignty, with coverage characterizing the corridor as a "proposal accepted by Oman on Iranian terms" rather than a product of external mediation pressure. Press TV broadcast segments describing the framework as a "humanitarian transit arrangement" consistent with Iranian legal positions on UNCLOS passage rights through the strait. IRNA reported FM Araghchi's Tehran press conference statement that the framework "does not prejudice Iran's rights under international law." → supports <span class="cite">N2</span> without move (resolved YES)</p>
      <p>Kayhan — the hardliner daily supervised by the Supreme Leader's office — ran no front-page commentary on the Oman transit corridor, an absence observed by Iran International as consistent with IRGC-affiliated factions' documented skepticism of the framework. State media carried no confirmation of a direct Mojtaba Khamenei public appearance in the August 26-28 window. IRIB reported that "the Supreme Leader's office" issued procedural guidance on the Oman negotiations without naming Mojtaba Khamenei as the issuing authority. Fars News published a claim that Munir's Aug 24-25 Tehran visit included a private meeting with "senior leadership" — a phrase carried without attribution to a named official or foreign government source. → supports <span class="cite">N4</span> without move</p>
      <p>AEOI spokesperson Behrouz Kamalvandi gave no public statement on enrichment levels or IAEA access restoration in the August 26-28 window. No Iranian state media outlet reported IAEA monitoring resumption or any downblending activity under international supervision. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

